<title>USA: Delta expands code-share agreement.</title>
<headline>Delta expands code-share agreement.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines said Wednesday that it won approval for an expanded code-share agreement with Sabena, Swissair and Austrian.</p>
<p>Beginning June 1, the three carriers will purchase seats on daily Delta flights to 30 U.S. cities beyond Delta's international gateways in New York, Cincinnati and Atlanta.</p>
<p>In addition to the 30 U.S. cities offered via Delta service, Delta will purchase seats on Sabena flights from Brussels to Oslo, Glasgow, London City, Leeds, Geneva, and Basel; on Swissair flights from Zurich to Geneva; and on Austrian flights from Vienna to Warsaw.</p>
</text>
